---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ReportCard from '../components/ReportCard.astro';
import CtaBand from '../components/CtaBand.astro';
---

<Base
  title="How ScamPrep works: safe practice scams and coaching"
  description="Realistic practice scams by phone and email, briefings on the newest scams, and a quarterly Resilience Report. See exactly how a scam fire drill works."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <p class="kicker">How it works</p>
      <h1>Receive drills, get coached, see progress.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        A fire drill isn't a lecture, it's a simulation that builds reflexes for the real thing. Here's what happens after you enroll in ScamPrep.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <!-- One connected timeline: each step shown with its artifact (all
           simulated, per the brand rule) instead of a card grid. -->
      <ol class="drill-line">
        <li>
          <span class="drill-line__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="2.5" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="m8.5 9.5 2.5 2.5 4.5-5" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M8 17h8" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <div class="drill-line__body">
            <div>
              <h3>Enroll with consent.</h3>
              <p>
                You sign up and your loved one opts in, always. Tell us a bit about them (email, phone, the scams they've seen before). They are up and running in two minutes, and there's nothing for them to install.
              </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="mock" aria-label="Simulated enrollment confirmation">
              <p class="mock__tag">Simulated enrollment notice</p>
              <div class="mock__card mock__card--consent">
                <span class="blip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                <p>Mary accepted her invitation. Drills begin this week.</p>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="drill-line__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2.5" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="m3.8 7.5 8.2 6 8.2-6" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <div class="drill-line__body">
            <div>
              <h3>We run safe, realistic drills.</h3>
              <p>
                On an unpredictable schedule, we send practice versions of the same scams circulating right now, by email, text, and phone. Drills are modeled on the latest tactics reported to the FBI and FTC.
              </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="mock" aria-label="Simulated drill email">
              <p class="mock__tag">Simulated drill email</p>
              <div class="mock__card">
                <p class="mock__meta">Cedar Bank Security · alerts@cedarbank-verify.co</p>
                <p class="mock__subject">Unusual sign-in detected — verify within 24 hours</p>
                <span class="mock__btn" aria-hidden="true">Verify my account</span>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="drill-line__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3a6 6 0 0 0-3.8 10.6c.6.600.9 1.300.9 2.1V16h5.8v-.3c0-.8.3-1.500.9-2.1A6 6 0 0 0 12 3z" fill="#F0A11C" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M9.5 19h5M10.5 21.5h3" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <div class="drill-line__body">
            <div>
              <h3>Coaching in the moment when they slip.</h3>
              <p>
                If your loved one clicks, nothing bad happens. A friendly page opens instead, providing a specific, usable lesson in thirty seconds. No lecture, no shame. Research shows this moment is when the lesson sticks.
              </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="mock" aria-label="Simulated coaching screen">
              <p class="mock__tag">Simulated coaching moment</p>
              <div class="mock__card mock__card--coach">
                <p class="mock__coach-head"><span class="blip blip--alert" aria-hidden="true"></span>This was a ScamPrep practice drill.</p>
                <p>Real banks never ask you to “verify” through an email link. Here are the three tells you can check in five seconds…</p>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="drill-line__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-8.5L6 20.8V17H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M7.5 8.5h9M7.5 12h5" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <div class="drill-line__body">
            <div>
              <h3>Briefings on the newest scams.</h3>
              <p>
                Alongside the drills, quick snippets on what's newly circulating and the tells to
                look for, sent through the channels they already use. Each one takes less than two
                minutes to read. Because briefings refresh continuously from what's reported to the
                FBI and FTC, recipients hear about new scams while they're still new.
              </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="mock" aria-label="Simulated briefing">
              <p class="mock__tag">Simulated briefing</p>
              <div class="mock__card">
                <p class="mock__meta">ScamPrep heads-up · Quick read, and always current</p>
                <p>A new IRS scam is making the rounds. The tell: they threaten arrest unless you pay right away. The IRS never calls to threaten arrest or demand immediate payment.</p>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </li>
        <li>
          <span class="drill-line__icon" aria-hidden="true"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="3" width="14" height="18" rx="2.5" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M9 17v-2M12 17v-5M15 17V9" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
          <div class="drill-line__body">
            <div>
              <h3>You get the Resilience Report.</h3>
              <p>
                Every quarter: drills we ran, which were caught, which were missed, and their scam resilience trend over time. Proof the practice is working, and an early look at any type of scam that keeps getting through.
              </p>
            </div>
            <aside class="mock" aria-label="Illustrative report excerpt">
              <p class="mock__tag">Illustrative report excerpt</p>
              <div class="mock__card mock__card--report">
                <div class="mock__row">
                  <span class="blip" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span>Fake bank “account locked” email</span>
                  <span class="mock__result">reported</span>
                </div>
                <div class="mock__row">
                  <span class="blip blip--alert" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                  <span>Fake bank text</span>
                  <span class="mock__result mock__result--alert">responded &amp; coached</span>
                </div>
                <p class="mock__status">Status: <strong>Mostly strong ↑</strong></p>
              </div>
            </aside>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>What a drill actually looks like</h2>
      <div class="drill-ex">
        <span class="drill-ex__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="5" width="18" height="14" rx="2.5" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="m3.8 7.5 8.2 6 8.2-6" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
        <p>
        <strong>The “account locked” email.</strong> Dad gets an email that looks like it's from a
        bank: <em>“Unusual sign-in detected. Verify your account within 24 hours.”</em> If he
        pauses, checks the sender, and deletes or reports it, that's a win on his Resilience Report. If
        he clicks, a calm page opens: “This was a ScamPrep practice drill. Real banks never ask you
        to ‘verify’ through an email link. Here are the three tells you can check in five seconds.”
        Total time: under a minute.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-ex">
        <span class="drill-ex__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 16.4v2.7a1.9 1.9 0 0 1-2.1 1.9 18.6 18.6 0 0 1-8.1-2.9 18.3 18.3 0 0 1-5.6-5.6A18.6 18.6 0 0 1 2.3 4.3 1.9 1.9 0 0 1 4.2 2.3h2.7a1.9 1.9 0 0 1 1.9 1.6c.1.9.3 1.800.7 2.6a1.9 1.9 0 0 1-.4 2L8 9.6a15 15 0 0 0 5.6 5.6l1.1-1.1a1.9 1.9 0 0 1 2-.4c.8.3 1.700.6 2.600.7A1.9 1.9 0 0 1 21 16.4z" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
        <p>
        <strong>The practice “grandparent” call.</strong> The phone rings, and a voice that sounds
        like her grandson says he's been in an accident, needs money for bail, and please don't tell
        his parents. The voice is an AI clone, and the call is simulated. If she hangs up and calls
        his real number, that's a win on her Resilience Report. If she stays on the line, the voice
        drops the act: “This was a ScamPrep practice call. Scammers can copy a voice from a few
        seconds of audio. The counter-move: hang up and call the real number, every time.”
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="drill-ex">
        <span class="drill-ex__icon"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="26" height="26" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 4h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2v9a2 2 0 0 1-2 2h-8.5L6 20.8V17H5a2 2 0 0 1-2-2V6a2 2 0 0 1 2-2z" fill="#FBEFD3" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/><path d="M7.5 8.5h9M7.5 12h5" fill="none" stroke="#332B23" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></span>
        <p>
        <strong>The practice “Social Security” text.</strong> A text arrives: “SSA notice: your
        Social Security number has been suspended due to suspicious activity. Call this number
        within 24 hours to avoid losing benefits.” If she ignores it or reports it, that's a win. The
        moment she calls or taps, the coaching kicks in: “Social Security never suspends numbers,
        and never texts you to call back. The counter-move: hang up and call the number on
        ssa.gov, or ask a family member to check with you.”
        </p>
      </div>
      <p>
        <em>Every drill is modeled on current tactics reported to the FBI, FTC, and state regulators, updated monthly as scams evolve.</em>
      </p>

      <h2>The cadence of drills</h2>
      <p>
        Drills arrive on an unpredictable schedule: typically <strong>4–6 per month</strong>,
        mixed among real messages so the practice is honest. Unpredictability is the point. Real
        scams don't make appointments.
      </p>
      <p>
        Frequency and type of drills adapt to your loved one: more reinforcement on scam types
        they've missed, lighter touch once instincts are strong.
      </p>

      <h2>The briefings: a quiet drip of education</h2>
      <p>
        Alongside the drills, we send very brief snippets: the newest scams in circulation and
        the tells to look out for. Each one takes less than two minutes to read, and they're spaced
        over time so the warnings stay fresh instead of fading the way a one-time seminar does.
      </p>
      <p>
        Because drills and briefings refresh continuously based on reports to the FBI and FTC, the
        person you care about hears about new scams while they're still new, often before they've
        hit the local news.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap report-split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>What's in the Resilience Report</h2>
        <p>Delivered every three months to you and your loved one:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>Every drill we ran, and how it went: caught, ignored, or coached</li>
          <li>A plain-English resilience status ("strong," "mostly strong") and how it's trending over time</li>
          <li>The scam types we're reinforcing next, and why</li>
          <li>A quick briefing on the quarter's most-reported scams</li>
        </ul>
        <h2 style="margin-top: 1.6em;">A gentle early-warning system</h2>
        <p>
          Research finds performance on simulated scam tests correlates with memory and real-world
          risk. A gradual decline in resilience doesn't diagnose anything but can spark a helpful
          conversation by providing an early signal families often wish they'd had. We surface it
          quietly, privately, and only to you and the learner.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div><ReportCard tone="light" /></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section--tight section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card" style="border-left: 4px solid var(--amber);">
        <h3>Which channels drills use</h3>
        <p><strong>Email:</strong> on from day one.</p>
        <p>
          <strong>Text and phone:</strong> added with their express written consent. Includes
          AI-voice calls (also known as “deepfakes”) like the “grandparent scam.”
        </p>
        <p><strong>Paper mail:</strong> coming soon.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          Text and voice simulations are regulated under federal telemarketing law. We built our consent process to exceed those requirements.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    headline="Ready to run the first drill?"
    body="Join the early-access list to protect your loved one."
  />
</Base>

<style>
  /* Drill examples: a small channel icon beside each scenario. */
  .drill-ex { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 44px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 16px; align-items: start; margin: 0 0 1.1em; }
  .drill-ex p { margin: 0; }
  .drill-ex__icon {
    width: 44px; height: 44px; border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid; place-items: center;
    background: var(--color-surface); border: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--color-text);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .drill-ex__icon svg { width: 26px; height: 26px; }

  .report-split {
    display: grid;
    gap: 48px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  @media (min-width: 920px) {
    .report-split { grid-template-columns: 1.2fr 1fr; }
  }
  ul { padding-left: 1.2em; }
  ul li { margin-bottom: 0.5em; }

  /* ---------- Drill timeline: the four steps on one connected rail, each
     with its (simulated) artifact beside it. ---------- */
  .drill-line { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
  .drill-line li { position: relative; padding: 0 0 48px 64px; }
  .drill-line li:last-child { padding-bottom: 0; }
  .drill-line li::before {
    content: '';
    position: absolute;
    left: 21px;
    top: 48px;
    bottom: 4px;
    width: 1.5px;
    background: var(--color-border);
  }
  .drill-line li:last-child::before { display: none; }
  /* Each step is marked with its icon from the brand set. */
  .drill-line__icon {
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    top: -6px;
    width: 44px;
    height: 44px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    background: var(--color-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
  }
  .drill-line h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin: 0 0 8px; }
  .drill-line__body { display: grid; gap: 18px 56px; }
  @media (min-width: 880px) {
    .drill-line__body { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 400px); align-items: start; }
  }
  .drill-line__body > div > p { margin: 0; }

  /* Artifact mocks — simulated UI, sized like the report card's interior. */
  .mock { margin: 0; }
  .mock__tag {
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.3;
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin: 0 0 8px;
  }
  .mock__card {
    background: var(--white);
    /* Simulated artifacts are drawn with a walnut line, like the report. */
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-text);
    border-radius: var(--radius-ctrl);
    padding: 16px 18px;
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--gray-700);
  }
  .mock__card p { margin: 0; }
  .mock__card--consent { display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: flex-start; }
  .mock__card--consent .blip { margin-top: 5px; }
  .mock__meta { font-size: 0.8rem; color: var(--gray-500); }
  .mock__subject { font-weight: 700; color: var(--ink); margin: 4px 0 12px !important; }
  .mock__btn {
    display: inline-block;
    /* A button inside a simulated scam email: outlined, never a dark fill. */
    background: var(--color-surface);
    color: var(--color-text);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-control-border);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    padding: 6px 14px;
    border-radius: var(--radius-chip);
  }
  /* Coaching is dusk blue. */
  .mock__card--coach { background: var(--color-coach-bg); border-color: var(--color-coach-text); color: var(--color-text); }
  .mock__coach-head {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    align-items: center;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--color-coach-text);
    margin: 0 0 6px !important;
  }
  .mock__row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
    background: var(--paper-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--color-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-ctrl);
    padding: 7px 11px;
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .mock__row + .mock__row { margin-top: 6px; }
  .mock__row span:nth-child(2) { flex: 1; }
  .mock__result { font-size: 0.8125rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--amber-deep); white-space: nowrap; }
  .mock__result--alert { color: var(--color-coach-text); }
  .mock__status { margin: 12px 0 0 !important; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  .mock__status strong {
    background: var(--amber-tint);
    color: var(--amber-deep);
    padding: 3px 9px;
    border-radius: 6px;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
  }
</style>
